# Silent Night, strum and sing (repertoire plan: silent-night). Gruber's carol of 1818 in G, so
# every chord is a level-3 chord: G (320003), D7 (xx0212) and C (x32010).
# 6/8 is two slow beats a bar, each split in three: count "ONE two three FOUR five six".
# Tempo 75 quarters is a dotted quarter of 50.
# Your part, first time through (verse 1 in John Freeman Young's English): one downstrum on 1 and
# one on 4. Second time (verse 1 in Joseph Mohr's German): the thumb on the bass on 1 and 4, the
# fingers on strings 3, 2 and 1 in between: p i m, p a m (G: string 6 then string 4; C: string 5
# then string 4; D7: string 4 both times).
# Harmony: G for "Silent night, holy night", D7 then G for "All is calm, all is bright", C then G
# for each of the next two lines, D7 then G for "Sleep in heavenly peace", G, D7, G at the end.
# The tune (second track) in first position, from low G (string 6 fret 3) up to C (string 2
# fret 1), with the note values of the
# usual hymnal version (twice those of Gruber's own 6/8). "Si-", "ho-", "-ther", the first "peace"
# and the second "Sleep" each take two notes.
title: Silent Night
id: silent-night
composer: Franz Xaver Gruber; words by Joseph Mohr
source: Carol of 1818; German words by Joseph Mohr, English words by John Freeman Young (1859); arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Gruber died in 1863, Mohr in 1848, Young in 1885); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: strumming, fingerpicking, 6/8, christmas, carol, lyrics
tempo: 75
time: 6/8
key: G

